; DOMAIN: mathematics/number-theory/motives [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-01]; Claim: Motives are a universal cohomology theory for algebraic varieties, unifying various cohomology theories (Betti, de Rham, l-adic, crystalline) via a system of realization functors and a conjectural abelian category. Key concepts: pure motives (Grothendieck), defined via algebraic cycles modulo adequate equivalence relations (rational, algebraic, homological, numerical); the category of motives as a pseudo-abelian tensor category; the Standard Conjectures (Kleinman) predicting that homological and numerical equivalence coincide; the Tannakian formalism giving motives a Galois-theoretic structure; the motivic Galois group generalizing the classical Galois group; mixed motives (Voevodsky) via triangulated categories and the derived category of motives; the motive of a point as the unit object; the motive of a curve and its relation to its Jacobian; the motivic L-function specializing to all cohomological L-functions; the motivic decomposition of the diagonal. Bridges to zeta_function (motivic L-functions), automorphic_forms (motivic Langlands), category_theory (Tannakian categories), and algebraic_geometry ( Chow groups, cycle class maps).;; Pure motive: defined via algebraic cycles modulo adequate equivalence relation, forms pseudo-abelian tensor category
(|- ((==> (&& (--> AlgebraicVariety $X) (--> AdequateEquivalence $E) (--> AlgebraicCycles $C $X) (--> Modulo $C $E) (--> PseudoAbelianTensor (CategoryOf $M)))) (--> PureMotive $M $X $E)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Standard Conjectures (Kleinman): homological equivalence coincides with numerical equivalence on algebraic cycles
(|- ((==> (&& (--> AlgebraicVariety $X) (--> HomologicalEquivalence $H) (--> NumericalEquivalence $N) (--> Coincide $H $N))) (--> StandardConjectures $X)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Tannakian formalism: category of motives over a field is a neutral Tannakian category, equivalent to representations of an affine group scheme
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Field $k) (--> CategoryOf $M (MotivesOver $k)) (--> NeutralTannakianCategory $M) (--> EquivalentTo $M (RepresentationsOf $G)))) (--> TannakianFormalism $M $G)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Motivic Galois group: affine group scheme whose representations recover motives, generalizes classical Galois group
(|- ((==> (&& (--> AffineGroupScheme $G) (--> TannakianCategory $M) (--> MotivesOver $k) (--> EquivalentTo $M (RepresentationsOf $G)))) (--> MotivicGaloisGroup $G $k)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Mixed motives: triangulated category (Voevodsky) providing derived framework, extends pure motives to non-smooth or open varieties
(|- ((==> (&& (--> TriangulatedCategory $D) (--> Field $k) (--> DerivedCategory $D (MotivesOver $k)) (--> Extends $D (PureMotive)))) (--> MixedMotive $D $k)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Motive of a point: unit object in the category of motives, corresponds to trivial 1-dimensional representation of motivic Galois group
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Motive $M) (--> UnitObject $M (CategoryOf $C)) (--> Corresponds $M (TrivialRepresentation)))) (--> MotiveOfPoint $M)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Motivic L-function: specializes to all cohomological L-functions, attached to pure motives via Euler product over primes
(|- ((==> (&& (--> PureMotive $M) (--> Field $k) (--> Function $L) (--> Equals (Apply $L $s) (ProductOver $p (LocalFactor $L $p $M))) (--> SpecializesTo $L (CohomologicalLFunctions)))) (--> MotivicLFunction $M $L)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
